## Why This Is Asked

Rationale: tests end-to-end ingestion, schema evolution in a multi-tenant IoT lake, data quality, and handling late data with canaries.

## Key Concepts

- Glue Schema Registry and Avro evolution
- Nested Avro schemas and optional fields
- Kinesis Data Streams + Glue ETL (Spark) + Parquet in S3
- Glue Data Catalog and partitioning by day
- Data quality checks, dedup, and late-arrival handling
- Canary testing and cost/latency trade-offs between Glue vs EMR Spark

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: evolution-safe defaults for missing fields
function applyDefaults(record, schema) {
  const out = {};
  for (const f of schema.fields) {
    if (record.hasOwnProperty(f.name)) out[f.name] = record[f.name];
    else if (f.default !== undefined) out[f.name] = f.default;
    else out[f.name] = null;
  }
  return out;
}
```

